<title>SWITZERLAND: EMU will not boost HSBC Asia forex trade - chairman.</title>
<headline>EMU will not boost HSBC Asia forex trade - chairman.</headline>
<dateline>INTERLAKEN, Switzerland 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>HSBC Holdings group chairman Sir William Purves said on Monday he did not expect the advent of the euro to boost HSBC's turnover in Asian currencies.</p>
<p>Purves told Reuters Financial Television (RFTV) that he believed the European single currency would go ahead, but Britain would be unlikely to belong to it at the beginning.</p>
<p>&quot;So as far as we are concerned, the euro will be just another currency and one in which we will be very actively involved,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Asked whether HSBC would conduct more forex trades in Asian currencies after the launch of economic and monetary union (EMU), Purves said: &quot;I don't see much change in the turnover of Asian currencies following the euro.&quot;</p>
<p>There was some danger the recent pressure on the Thai baht could spill over into other Asian currencies. But he praised the efforts of Asian central banks to prevent this and said it was a good thing that &quot;one or two fingers have been burned&quot; as a result of the Thai authorities taking steps to steady the baht.</p>
<p>-- Stephen Nisbet, Zurich editorial +411 631 7340</p>
